<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A hard break inside a cell starts a line of its own, whatever room the column has left.

  Calc stores such a cell as an EditTextObject rather than as a string — a BIFF or
  SpreadsheetML string holding U+000A becomes CELLTYPE_EDIT (XclImpStringHelper::SetToDocument,
  sc/source/filter/excel/xihelper.cxx:245-258) — and ScOutputData sends every edit cell to
  DrawEdit, where each paragraph is a line.

  Column A is 6cm, far wider than any of the short strings in it, which is the case that
  matters: a layouter that only breaks when the text overruns its column draws all three
  paragraphs of row 1 on one line and is wrong by two lines. Column B is 2cm, so its strings
  break inside a paragraph as well as at the paragraph's end.

  LibreOffice 24.2.7.2's own PDF of this file, read with `pdftotext -bbox`, is what each row
  below claims. The line pitch throughout is 11.197 pt.

  Row 1  three paragraphs that fit the column between them  — three lines: 57.73, 68.93, 80.12
  Row 2  the same three, in a cell that does not wrap       — three lines: 92.74, 103.93, 115.13
  Row 3  a paragraph, an empty one, a paragraph             — Golf at 127.83 and Hotel at 150.22,
                                                              two pitches apart: the empty
                                                              paragraph takes a line
  Row 4  no break at all, and wider than its 2cm column     — two lines, the control for the
                                                              wrap itself
  Row 5  two paragraphs, the first wider than its column    — three lines: Mike / November /
                                                              Oscar Papa
  Row 6  three paragraphs, the first bold                   — the rich-cell path, three lines

  Row 2 is here as a measurement rather than as an assertion, and the test says so: ODF's
  importer disagrees with the other two about it. It makes a multi-paragraph edit cell whatever
  the wrap option says, which is the three lines above. BIFF and SpreadsheetML both fold the
  same content onto one paragraph when the cell does not wrap — `SetSingleLine(!GetLineBreak())`
  in sc/source/filter/excel/xihelper.cxx:250-256, and `bSingleLine = !mbWrapText` in
  sc/source/filter/oox/sheetdatabuffer.cxx:120-135, which a string holding U+000A always
  reaches because RichString::extractPlainString refuses it (richstring.cxx:363-378). Since the
  sheets corpus is entirely .xls and .xlsx, what we do — one line — is what those two ask for,
  and only the ODF side is unimplemented.
-->
<office:document xmlns:office="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:office:1.0"
 xmlns:style="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:style:1.0"
 xmlns:text="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:text:1.0"
 xmlns:table="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:table:1.0"
 xmlns:fo="urn:oasis:names:tc:opendocument:xmlns:xsl-fo-compatible:1.0"
 office:version="1.3" office:mimetype="application/vnd.oasis.opendocument.spreadsheet">
 <office:automatic-styles>
  <style:style style:name="co1" style:family="table-column">
   <style:table-column-properties style:column-width="6cm"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="co2" style:family="table-column">
   <style:table-column-properties style:column-width="2cm"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="ceWrap" style:family="table-cell">
   <style:table-cell-properties fo:wrap-option="wrap" style:vertical-align="top"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="ceFlat" style:family="table-cell">
   <style:table-cell-properties fo:wrap-option="no-wrap" style:vertical-align="top"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:style style:name="tBold" style:family="text">
   <style:text-properties fo:font-weight="bold"/>
  </style:style>
  <style:page-layout style:name="pm1">
   <style:page-layout-properties fo:page-width="21cm" fo:page-height="29.7cm"
    fo:margin-left="2cm" fo:margin-right="2cm" fo:margin-top="2cm" fo:margin-bottom="2cm"
    style:print-orientation="portrait"/>
  </style:page-layout>
 </office:automatic-styles>
 <office:master-styles>
  <style:master-page style:name="Default" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/>
 </office:master-styles>
 <office:body>
  <office:spreadsheet>
   <table:table table:name="Probe">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="co1"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="co2"/>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p>Alpha</text:p><text:p>Bravo</text:p><text:p>Charlie</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>one</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceFlat" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p>Delta</text:p><text:p>Echo</text:p><text:p>Foxtrot</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>two</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p>Golf</text:p><text:p/><text:p>Hotel</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>three</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>four</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p>India Juliett Kilo Lima</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>five</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p>Mike November</text:p><text:p>Oscar Papa</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="ceWrap" office:value-type="string"
      ><text:p><text:span text:style-name="tBold">Quebec</text:span></text:p
      ><text:p>Romeo</text:p><text:p>Sierra</text:p></table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell office:value-type="string"><text:p>six</text:p></table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
  </office:spreadsheet>
 </office:body>
</office:document>
